# Life and Limb (turn 1), then Blood Moon (turn 5); both apply in layer 4 (CR 613.1d).
# - Taiga and Dryad Arbor are nonbasic Forests. Applying Blood Moon makes them Mountains and not Forests, which changes
#   what Life and Limb applies to, so Life and Limb's effect depends on Blood Moon's (CR 613.8a) and waits until after it
#   (CR 613.8b), though it is older. After the Moon neither is a Forest or a Saproling, so Life and Limb does not apply to
#   them at all: Taiga is a plain Land - Mountain, no creature; Dryad Arbor is a Land Creature - Dryad Mountain, 1/1 and
#   green by its own card, and no Saproling. (Applied in timestamp order, Life and Limb would first make them Saprolings,
#   and they would stay Saproling creatures under the Moon.) Before the Moon both are 1/1 green Saproling Forests.
# - Woodland Changeling is a Saproling (Changeling, CR 702.73a). Life and Limb makes it a Forest land; Blood Moon applies to
#   it only once it is a land, so here Blood Moon's effect depends on Life and Limb's and applies after it: it is a
#   Mountain, no longer a Forest, but still a Saproling, so Life and Limb still applies - a 1/1 green Land Creature, every
#   creature type and Mountain, that taps for {R} and not {G} (CR 305.6, 305.7).

[Bot1 Deck]
Taiga
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Life and Limb
Woodland Changeling
Dryad Arbor
Blood Moon
Plains
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x30

